# Free LLM providers — generated from registry.yaml, do not edit by hand.
# Fill the keys you use, then `source` this file. Every endpoint is
# OpenAI-compatible: point any SDK/agent at the base URL next to the key.

# ── Google AI Studio (Gemini API) — base: https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/ · get a key: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
export GOOGLE_AI_STUDIO_API_KEY=""
#    note: pass the key as Bearer

# ── OpenRouter (free models) — base: https://openrouter.ai/api/v1 · get a key: https://openrouter.ai/settings/keys
export OPENROUTER_API_KEY=""
#    note: Use IDs with the :free suffix; their input and output prices are zero. openrouter/free chooses a free model automatically. LiquidAI advises against agentic coding with lfm-2.5-2.6b. For Claude Code, set ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api, leave ANTHROPIC_API_KEY empty and use a :free ID as ANTHROPIC_MODEL.

# ── Groq — base: https://api.groq.com/openai/v1 · get a key: https://console.groq.com/keys
export GROQ_API_KEY=""
#    note: the chat models Groq's own Free Plan Limits table names; its safeguard and prompt-guard classifiers, compound systems, whisper and orpheus rows are left out

# ── Kilo Code — no key needed · base: https://api.kilo.ai/api/gateway
#    note: Use free IDs without a key; metered IDs require sign-in. kilo-auto/free and openrouter/free choose a free model automatically. LiquidAI advises against agentic coding with lfm-2.5-2.6b.

# ── Requesty — base: https://router.requesty.ai/v1 · get a key: https://app.requesty.ai/api-keys
export REQUESTY_API_KEY=""
#    note: Free-plan IDs are priced zero and have no expired retirement date; they carry no :free suffix. NVIDIA rows disclose training use and 30-day retention. For Claude Code, set ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://router.requesty.ai, or https://router.eu.requesty.ai for EU residency.

# ── NVIDIA NIM (build.nvidia.com) — base: https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1 · get a key: https://build.nvidia.com
export NVIDIA_NIM_API_KEY=""
#    note: Use available chat endpoints marked Free Endpoint. /v1/models also lists older IDs without a free mark, so catalog membership alone does not establish free access.

# ── AIHubMix (free models) — base: https://aihubmix.com/v1 · get a key: https://aihubmix.com/token
export AIHUBMIX_API_KEY=""
#    note: The listed -free IDs are zero-priced. intern-s2-free serves Intern-S2-Preview 35B; union-alpha-free is a stealth model, and k2.6-code-preview-free describes kimi-for-coding. For Claude Code, use https://aihubmix.com as ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL.

# ── Z.ai (Zhipu GLM) — base: https://api.z.ai/api/paas/v4 · get a key: https://z.ai/manage-apikey/apikey-list
export ZAI_GLM_API_KEY=""
#    note: the ids are the chat completion reference's own, where glm-4.7-flash and glm-4.5-flash sit in its model enum; Coding-Plan keys use https://api.z.ai/api/coding/paas/v4 instead. The Claude Code guide sets ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL to https://api.z.ai/api/anthropic with "your_zai_api_key" as the token and names Coding-Plan ids (glm-5.3, glm-5.3-flash); whether the free Flash ids answer on that route is not stated, and the route answers 401 keyless (2026-09-05)

# ── Cloudflare Workers AI — base: https://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/ai/v1 · get a key: https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens
export CLOUDFLARE_WORKERS_AI_API_KEY=""
#    note: substitute {account_id} with your Cloudflare account ID

# ── Routeway — base: https://api.routeway.ai/v1 · get a key: https://routeway.ai/dashboard/keys
export ROUTEWAY_API_KEY=""
#    note: Only IDs ending :free are free; the same catalog meters Claude, GPT and other paid models. Some zero-priced community fine-tunes are intended for expressive writing and roleplay.

# ── LLM7.io — base: https://api.llm7.io/v1 · get a key: https://dash.llm7.io
export LLM7_API_KEY=""
#    note: Use a free dashboard token for the documented allowance. The listed IDs are marked turbo with usage_based_only false in the catalog; their authenticated availability has not been independently confirmed.

# ── LLMTR — base: https://llmtr.com/v1 · get a key: https://llmtr.com/dashboard/api-keys
export LLMTR_API_KEY=""
#    note: New accounts have a reduced shared free-model allowance during their first 24 hours. Nemotron Ultra -262k is metered. Grant Heabsy data-transfer consent in Settings → Data-transfer consents; its stream is buffered until completion and reasoning_effort is unsupported. For Nemotron3.5 Super VL, omit reasoning_effort; reasoning: false disables thinking. Beam always reasons; reasoning_effort defaults to max and accepts low, medium, high, xhigh or max. Set max_tokens to bound the answer, including reasoning.
# heabsy/qwen3.8-27b-heabsy-free: free until 2026-11-02 00:00+03:00;
# https://llmtr.com/models/heabsy/qwen3.8-27b-heabsy-free
# reflection/beam-1.0-501b-a23b: free until 2026-10-22 23:59+03:00;
# https://llmtr.com/models/reflection/beam-1.0-501b-a23b

# ── LLM Tech — no account needed · base: https://api.llmtech.eu/v1
#    the vendor prints this key for anyone at https://llmtech.eu/docs/ — put your own in its place if you have one
export LLMTECH_API_KEY="lt-trial-ba1ef28c6d32ed6980678d8d"
#    note: since 2026-09-24 "Reasoning is off unless a request asks for it with reasoning_effort or enable_thinking", and `reasoning_effort` takes low, medium or xhigh. Cline lists LLM Tech among its built-in providers; Claude Code "needs a translating proxy", LiteLLM in the vendor's own example

# ── Vercel AI Gateway — base: https://ai-gateway.vercel.sh/v1 · get a key: https://vercel.com/dashboard/ai-gateway/api-keys
export VERCEL_AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=""
#    note: Use exact zero-priced IDs; metered routes spend gateway credit. For Beam, use reflection/beam-free: it stops when free access ends. The regular reflection/beam route can charge at provider rates. Reflection's terms and privacy policy apply. For Claude Code, set ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://ai-gateway.vercel.sh and leave ANTHROPIC_API_KEY empty.

# ── Hetzner Inference API — base: https://inference.hetzner.com/api/v1 · get a key: https://experiments.hetzner.com/inference
export HETZNER_INFERENCE_API_KEY=""
#    note: both ids are 262K-context and take text and images; /v1/models, /v1/completions and /v1/chat/completions are the whole surface. The key is minted in the Inference tab of experiments.hetzner.com, which is a client-rendered page behind a Hetzner login — the readable copy of the terms is the docs page this row probes

# ── Alibaba Cloud Model Studio (DashScope, international) — base: https://dashscope-intl.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1 · get a key: https://modelstudio.console.alibabacloud.com
export ALIBABA_MODEL_STUDIO_API_KEY=""
#    note: Singapore (international) endpoint; keys are region-specific. Call the exact IDs listed here. Enable Free Quota Only per model in the console to stop calls when its grant ends.

# ── BazaarLink — base: https://api.bazaarlink.ai/v1 · get a key: https://bazaarlink.ai/keys
export BAZAARLINK_API_KEY=""
#    note: only the two :free ids and auto:free cost nothing — the plain qwen3.7-flash beside the first is the metered twin (from $0.03/$0.13 per 1M, with higher long-prompt tiers), and deepseek-v4-flash-0731free without the suffix is metered at $0.20/$0.40. auto:free picks a free model for you, and on a funded account it can fall through to the paid routing table "unless paid fallback is disabled"

# ── Inferbase — base: https://api.inferbase.ai/v1 · get a key: https://inferbase.ai/docs/getting-started/quickstart
export INFERBASE_API_KEY=""
#    note: Create an account and a gateway API key. The auto ID routes among models eligible under the key policy; the response names the model that served the request. Managed usage spends a shared budget, so no model is independently free. The vendor documents OpenAI chat and Anthropic Messages tool loops; authenticated generation has not been checked here.

# ── Nous Portal (Hermes Agent) — base: https://inference-api.nousresearch.com/v1 · get a key: https://portal.nousresearch.com
export NOUS_PORTAL_API_KEY=""
#    note: Select a :free model and use your Nous Portal key; paid variants are outside the free plan. The Step 5 catalog has served different token limits; check its current model entry before choosing a large context or output budget.

# ── Regolo AI — base: https://api.regolo.ai/v1 · get a key: https://dashboard.regolo.ai
export REGOLO_API_KEY=""
#    note: GET /v1/models is public and needs no key, but it publishes ids only — the prices and the trial terms are on the pricing page this row probes. brick-v1-beta is the one id priced at zero on that page, and it is Brick's prompt-complexity classifier rather than a coding model; brick-complexity-pro, Included under Core, is the Brick router itself, which picks a model for you

# ── Token Harbor — base: https://tokenharbor.ai/v1 · get a key: https://tokenharbor.ai/dashboard/api-keys
export TOKEN_HARBOR_API_KEY=""
#    note: The :free suffix selects the free route, which has to be switched on in the dashboard first. /v1/models needs a key; use the IDs listed under Free on the Models page. For Claude Code the docs say "a free account works" and "every gateway model works on both endpoints".

# ── TokenRouter (PaleBlueDot) — base: https://api.tokenrouter.com/v1 · get a key: https://www.tokenrouter.com/console/token
export TOKENROUTER_API_KEY=""
#    note: Use the zero-priced free-model ID in the default group. PaleBlueDot AI runs tokenrouter.com; similarly named gateways on other TLDs are separate services and their keys do not work here.

# ── Mistral Studio — base: https://api.mistral.ai/v1 · get a key: https://console.mistral.ai/api-keys
